%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sovngarde
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Huh.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708828
    - rid: 4927988726549708829
    - rid: 4927988726549708830
    - rid: 4927988726549708831
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Despite all of the snow, this place is actually pretty temperate.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Not sure whether to attribute that to this place being Nord heaven-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Or because Aetherius could be considered a place of pure and infinite
      energy.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Since, you know, it's where magic comes from.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Guess I'll get moving...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah. The fog.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708832
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I <i>could</i> get rid of this fog with the Clear Skies shout...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Or I could not do that!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The NPCs that are lost in there complaining about not being to make their
      way to Shor's Hall are a bunch of shmucks-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: You sort of just have to keep going straight from where you arrive.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... assuming the dead arrive at the same spot that I did.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Which may not be true now that I'm thinking about it...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hrm.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Anyway, it should just be a nice and easy walk to the Whalebone Bridge-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah-!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708889
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: My nose...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah crap, is that blood!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hopefully they have cotton balls at the Hall of Valor...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Tripping right onto my face not withstanding, the trek was as easy as
      I remembered.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708890
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: What brings you, wayfarer grim, to wander here, in Sovngarde, souls-end,
      Shor's gift to honored dead?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708891
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's this pesky World-Eater problem I'm sure you've heard of; I'm
      here to deal with that.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: A fateful errand. No few have chafed to face the Worm since first he
      set his soul-snare here at Sovngarde's threshold.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: But Shor restrained our wrathful onslaught- perhaps, deep counseled,
      your doom he foresaw.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, yeah.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Listen, I know that entrance to the Hall of Valor requires beating you
      in combat-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So can we skip the whole "by whose right do you seek entry" thing?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: Special permissions must be granted for those who would dare enter Shor's
      Hall while still belonging to life.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Haaahh...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Fine.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: <i>By right of blood. I am the dragonborn</i>.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Happy?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: It has been too long since last I've faced a doom-driven hero of the
      dragon blood.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Can we just fight now?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: Very well.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Tsun draws his axe to give {mc} the warrior's test.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118219413979188
    - rid: 1790118219413979189
    - rid: 1790118219413979190
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: You fought well. I find you worthy.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118219413979240
    - rid: 1790118219413979241
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: It is long since one of the living has entered here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67745692676d04c4ba502c64a1dbfa23, type: 2}
    dialog: May Shor's favor follow you and your errand.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Tsun steps to the side, letting me walk across the Whalebone Bridge.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118219413979242
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: It's a bit outrageous that over the course of the entirety of creation,
      Shor has never invested in an <i>actual</i> bridge.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Whale skeletons aren't exactly made to be walked upon.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Managed to make it across-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118219413979243
    - rid: 1790118219413979244
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Despite the best efforts of the skeleton trying to catch my ankles.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: No point in wasting anymore time, I've got to meet up with the ancient
      Nords shown in the Elder Scroll.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118219413979245
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
